From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Benjamin Gregoire <Benjamin.Gregoire@inria.fr>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 17:47:20 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] armv8a: add BFC, BFI, BFXIL, SBFX and UBFX
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The bitfield aliases clear (BFC), insert (BFI), insert at the low end
(BFXIL) or extract with sign or zero extension (SBFX, UBFX) a field given
by its bit position and width, in both the W and X forms. The field must
lie within the register: the semantics is undefined otherwise, and the
safety conditions of the descriptors state the bounds. All five are DIT
(BFM, SBFM and UBFM).

This completes the scalar data-processing instructions of the backend.
The variable-shift mnemonics ASRV, LSLV, LSRV and RORV are not provided:
their only form is the register form of ASR, LSL, LSR and ROR, which the
backend already provides.

Co-authored-by: Côme LE BRETON <come.le-breton@inria.fr>
(cherry picked from commit 523725574d9837fa731107b28aaa7788db6341f4)
